.\n3. Other developing moves like `N: b8-c6` ignore the free material and allow White to retreat the Bishop.\n\nReason: Capturing the undefended Bishop grants a decisive material advantage. `P: b7-a6` is chosen over `N: b8-a6` because it opens the b-file for the rook and avoids placing the knight on a passive square.\n\nAnswer: P: b7-a6'}
