es the Bishop to a central square where it is safe from pawn attacks and not easily trapped. It preserves the full material advantage (Queen up) without allowing White any counterplay or tactical complexities.\n\nReason: Since Black is already winning by a large margin (extra Queen), the optimal strategy is to play safely and avoid giving away pieces or entering complications. Moving the Bishop to e6 saves it from the current threat and places it on a secure square, consolidating the win.\n\nAnswer: B: g4-e6"}
