ately captured by the White Knight at b1. Giving up the active Knight is unnecessary given the other options.\n3.  **N: e4-g5**: This provides a check, but allows the King more escape squares (like g3). It is less restrictive than the Queen check.\n4.  **B: f5-g4**: This checks the King but sacrifices the Bishop to the White King or Pawn at h3.\n\nReason: The move Q: d8-d3 is the best choice because it is a safe, forcing check that restricts the enemy King to a single, perilous square (f4). It utilizes the Queen's power and the support of the c4 pawn to set up a decisive mating attack without sacrificing any material.\n\nAnswer: Q: d8-d3"}
